          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Segal condition
            is a condition on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet \in \mathcal{C}^{\Delta^{op}}
            which says that each component
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n \geq 2} \in \mathcal{C}
            is obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \stackrel{\overset{\partial_0}{\to}}{\underset{\partial_1}{\to}} X_0
            by the
            = succeed "-fold" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+product"} fiber product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            which “glues”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            copies of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            end-to-end.
          %p
            Hence if one thinks of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            as a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            and of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1
            as a collection of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_\bullet
            satisfies the Segal condition precisely if each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n \geq 2}
            can be interpreted as the collection of sequences of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composable
            morphisms of length
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ForSimplicialObjects"} Definition – For simplicial objects
          %p
            Accordingly, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            is the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            which are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            of a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"}> strict
            )
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#NerveTheorem"}
            below. This is the observation due to
            %a{:href => "#Grothendieck61"} Grothendieck 1961
            as recalled in
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#Segal68"} Segal 1968
            %em nerve theorem
            (no relation to what is called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+theorem"} nerve theorem
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p It is useful to decompose this statement into its constituents as follows:
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            may be thought of as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(C)
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+law"} unital
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composition
            operation. This corresponds to a sequence of inclusions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mn 0
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (1 \stackrel{\overset{d_0}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{d_1}{\leftarrow}} 0) \hookrightarrow \Delta_0 \to \Delta
          %p
            into the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
            is the category of finite non-empty directed linear graphs:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graph"} directed graph
                is equivalently a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                on
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mover
                          %munder
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mn 1
                          %mover
                            %mo ←
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mn 0
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 \stackrel{\overset{d_0}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{d_1}{\leftarrow}} 0)
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                encodes via its face and degeneracy maps a kind of associative and unital composition – but not necessarily “of composable morphisms” if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{n\geq 2}
                is not given in the above fashion.
          %p
            In terms of this we can say that equipping a directed graph with the structure of a category is equivalent to asking for its pushforward along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo ←
                      %mrow
                        %msub
