                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Θ
                    %mn 0
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Θ
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^* X \colon \Theta_0^{op} \to \Theta^{op} \to \mathcal{C}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+site"} cellular site
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            there.
          %p
            The cellular objects that satisfy the Segal condition are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-category"} ∞-category
            objects (
            %a{:href => "#Berger"}> Berger
            ).
          %p
            The cellular spaces/ cellular simplicial sets/cellular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            that satisfy the Segal condition as a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} equivalence of ∞-groupoids
            is a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta_n-space"} Theta_n-space
            an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} (∞,n)-category
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#characterization_of_nerves_of_higher_categories Characterization of nerves of (higher) categories
          %h4#of_simplicial_nerves_of_small_categories Of simplicial nerves of small categories
          %p The archetypical role of the Segal condition is to make the following statement true.
          #NerveTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (nerve theorem)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              precisely if it satsfies the Segal conditions.
          %p
            This is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Grothendieck61"} Grothendieck 61
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Segal68"} Segal 1968
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              There is an entirely unrelated theorem in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              also often called “the”
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+theorem"} nerve theorem
          %h4#of_complete_segal_spaces Of complete Segal spaces
          %p
            By refining the above result from sets to
            = succeed "-groupoids," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pre-category+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} pre-category object in an (infinity,1)-category
          %h4#of_cellular_nerves_of_strict_categories
            Of cellular nerves of strict
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
          %p
            Similarly, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+set"} cellular set
            is the cellular nerve of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-category"} strict omega-category
            precisely if it satisfies the cellular Segal condition. (
            %a{:href => "#Berger"}> Berger
            ).
          %h4#of_cellular_models_of_categories
            Of cellular models of
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theta-space"} Theta-space
          %h3#InTermsOfSheafConditions In terms of sheaf conditions
          %p
            We discuss an equivalent formulation of the Segal condition in terms of notions in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos+theory"} (∞,1)-topos theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal language
            of toposes.
          %h4#InTermsOfSheafConditionForSimplicialObjects For simplicial objects and category objects
          %p
            We characterize below in prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CatAsPullback"}
            the category of categories as the pullback of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            along the inclusion of the topos of graphs into that of presheaves on finite linear graphs.
          %p First we state some preliminaries.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              The condition in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SegalCones"}
              superficially looks like a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              condition for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverings"} coverings
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[n]
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              subsequent copies of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]
              %em not
              form a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Δ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            %p
              For instance for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_1 \colon \Delta[1] \to \Delta[2]
              the map that sends the single edge of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[1]
              to the composite edge in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta[2]
              there is no way to “pull back” the cover
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{\Delta[1] \coprod \Delta[1] \stackrel{((0,1),(1,2))}{\to} \Delta[2]\}
            %p
              along this morphism, not even in the weak sense of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
            %p
              However, as this example also makes clear, the problem is precisely only with the morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              that are no injective on generating edges.
          %p Therefore consider instead the following:
          #FiniteLinearGraphsInAllGraphs.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Graph
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    j \colon \Delta_0 \hookrightarrow Graph
            %p
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graphs"} directed graphs
              on the linear graphs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo →
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0 \to 1 \to \cdots \to n\}
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Morphisms in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0
              have to send elementary edges to elementary edges. So there are
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  precisely
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0[1] \to \Delta_0[n]
              %li
                %p
                  precisely
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0[2] \to \Delta_0[n+1]
              %li
                %p
                  precisely
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_0[3] \to \Delta_0[n+2]
              %li
                %p etc.
          #ParallelMorphismCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mo ←
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    i
                    \\colon
                    (1 \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\leftarrow} 0) \hookrightarrow \Delta_0
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on the linear graphs with no edge and with one edge.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graphs"} directed graphs
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalently
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mo ←
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 \stackrel{\leftarrow}{\leftarrow} 0)
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParallelMorphismCategory"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Graph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ⇐
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Graph(\mathcal{C}) \simeq PSh((1 \Leftarrow 0), \mathcal{C})
                    \=
                    \\mathcal{C}^{(1 \Rightarrow 0)}
                    \\,.
          #AdjointTripleFromGraphs.num_prop
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mover
                        %munder
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo ←
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi i
                              %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi i
                            %mo !
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (i_! \dashv i^* \dashv i_*)
                    \\colon
                    \\mathcal{C}^{1 \Rightarrow 0}
                    \\stackrel{\overset{i_!}{\to}}{\stackrel{\overset{i^*}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{i_*}{\to}}}
                    \\mathcal{C}^{\Delta_0^{op}}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
              induced on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
              by the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              of def.
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ParallelMorphismCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*
              is given by precomposition with
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_!
              is left and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_*
              is right
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              along
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          #NerveOfGraph.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Graph
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mn 0
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_* \colon Graph(\mathcal{C}) \to \mathcal{C}^{\Delta_0^{op}}
              of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdjointTripleFromGraphs"}
              sends a graph
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 0
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_1 \stackrel{\overset{\partial_1}{\to}}{\underset{\partial_0}{\to}} X_0
              to the presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi i
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_*(X)
              which on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              is given by th iterated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
